# The shortcut builds each value where it shows it: `Section().show(heading)` is of `Section` and no class below, so the
# call runs the one `show` a `Section` runs, `Block.show`, named by the class it runs on, and is no choice. Nothing it
# runs raises.
route notes.report.report
step report/read_text
step report/Section()
step report/Section.show                                  # `Section().show(heading)`: one function

line entry > report call
line Disk(report.source) > report own
line report/read_text > _·heading@report/read_text value
line report/Section() > Section@report/Section() value
line Section@report/Section() > report/Section.show value
line _·heading@report/read_text > report/Section.show value
line report/Section.show > Screen own

home _·heading@report/read_text report
home Section@report/Section() report

side entry left
side Disk(report.source) left
side Screen right

# `Block().show(heading)` is of `Block` alone: `Block.show`, though `Boxed` overrides it below.
route notes.report.note
step note/read_text
step note/Block()
step note/Block.show

line entry > note call
line Disk(note.source) > note own
line note/read_text > _·heading@note/read_text value
line note/Block() > Block@note/Block() value
line Block@note/Block() > note/Block.show value
line _·heading@note/read_text > note/Block.show value
line note/Block.show > Screen own

home _·heading@note/read_text note
home Block@note/Block() note

side entry left
side Disk(note.source) left
side Screen right
